\p{The executable's loader needs 1.2 to 1.3 times the JVM's CPU after the first pass over its code, where it needed 1.33. A second of the difference is kernel time: the image's loader thread takes 0.76 million more page faults per pass than the JVM's, and its workers half a million where the JVM's take none. Per pass the image's loader thread executes 119.4 G instructions in 41.4 G cycles, 2.9 instructions per cycle, with 13.1 G cycles stalled on memory, 76 million last-level read misses, 33.7 million data TLB walks and 166 million mispredicted branches.}
}

