\tr{\td{rounds}\td{3}\td{2}\td{2}\td{2}}
}

\ul{
\li{\strong{An eighth of the loader's cycles for a thirtieth of its instructions.} The first pass took a fifth of the instructions and half as much of the time; this one takes 2 to 3.5 \% of the instructions and 12 to 15 \% of a load's cycles in user mode. The cycles were waiting: for the numbers of a line, and for the name index. The mispredicted branches go up by 3 to 8 \%: the end of a stretch of three line kinds is harder to guess than the end of a stretch of one.}
\li{\strong{The kernel's part is unchanged}, as section 3 says it must be: none of the two changes touches a page less.}
}
}

