\ul{
\li{\strong{The guard holds on both launchers.} The executable: the geometric mean goes down by 2.4 \%, and every corpus is faster, by 1.0 \% (reachability, whose load is 30 ms of a pass of 540 ms) to 3.6 \%; Mathlib 14.88 to 14.43 s. The JVM launcher: the geometric mean goes down by 1.9 \%; six corpora are 0.5 to 5.2 \% faster, con-leche is at +0.2 \% and reachability at +2.2 \%, with rounds of the base from 396 to 458 ms: the loader is 26 ms of this pass, and the difference is inside that scatter (the JVM launcher asks for huge pages, so its rounds also carry the state of the host's memory that section 7 describes, in base and candidate alike); eight further rounds on this corpus were queued and did not get a window. No corpus is more than 3 \% slower in either, and every pass of every round ended ACCEPT with every unit accepted.}
\li{\strong{The loader thread is busy 8 to 11 \% less} in the executable on seven corpora (cslib 5 \%), \strong{and the pass gets 1.8 to 3.6 \% shorter} on the corpora whose pass is their load (Init, Std, cedar): the thread then waits for the workers. It is busy for 76 to 87 \% of the candidate's pass on these three, where it was busy for 82 to 94 \% of the base's. On Mathlib the loader thread is busy 1.32 s less (13.10 to 11.78 s) and the pass is 0.45 s shorter; the CPU of the pass goes from 112.3 to 110.7 s.}
\li{\strong{Peak RSS} is the largest value of the three rounds. In the executable the rounds of base and candidate overlap on seven corpora (Mathlib round by round: 4,419 4,348 4,468 against 4,363 4,336 4,453 MiB; cslib 1,978 1,973 1,993 against 2,071 1,942 1,973 MiB), and cedar is 6 to 30 MiB, 1 to 4 \%, higher in every round (763 763 759 against 769 786 789 MiB). A likely cause, not verified: with a faster loader the workers lag further behind it, and more of what they have not checked yet is resident at the peak; the store itself is the same size, word for word. On the JVM launcher the differences are those of the collector from round to round (Mathlib 4,992 5,018 4,957 against 4,962 5,074 5,099 MiB).}
}
}

