}

\p{What the thread is now: a sixth kernel, a sixth scanner, and still a third the seven loads of section 2.3: the name table has gone from 8.7 to 5.4 \% of the thread, and the other six loads have grown from 22 to 26 \% of a thread that got shorter around them.}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.5 The scanner threads: is one still the default?}

\p{[The settings of a plain run](dec-EGMG) chose one scanner thread - the loader thread itself, scanning the mapped file - over two helper threads that tokenise and pack ahead of it, because beside eight workers on eight cores a helper takes a core from the checking; the first pass left the question open for a faster loader. The candidate executable with the default, with \code{\verb~|-X scan-threads=2~} and with \code{\verb~|-X scan-threads=0~} (no mapping: the file is read into the scan buffer), interleaved in one quiet window, two rounds, warm passes with 8 workers, the median later pass of a process:}

\table{
\tr{\th{candidate executable, warm pass}\th{1 (the default), s}\th{2 scanner threads, s}\th{none, plain read, s}\th{CPU of the pass, s: 1 / 2 / none}\th{peak RSS, MiB: 1 / 2 / none}\th{rounds, ms: 1 / 2 / none}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{0.641}\td{0.670 (+4.5 \%)}\td{0.648 (+1.2 \%)}\td{4.6 / 4.9 / 4.7}\td{390 / 528 / 382}\td{640 641 / 674 665 / 647 649}}
\tr{\td{navier-stokes-euler}\td{3.935}\td{4.568 (+16.1 \%)}\td{3.882 (-1.3 \%)}\td{29.1 / 31.7 / 29.2}\td{1,535 / 1,804 / 1,511}\td{3970 3899 / 4538 4598 / 3903 3861}}
\tr{\td{cslib}\td{5.208}\td{5.458 (+4.8 \%)}\td{5.224 (+0.3 \%)}\td{39.6 / 41.4 / 39.6}\td{2,006 / 2,230 / 2,059}\td{5245 5171 / 5472 5443 / 5252 5196}}
\tr{\td{Mathlib}\td{14.286}\td{15.009 (+5.1 \%)}\td{14.449 (+1.1 \%)}\td{110.0 / 115.6 / 111.1}\td{4,423 / 4,730 / 4,410}\td{14174 14397 / 14889 15128 / 14463 14434}}
}

\ul{
\li{\strong{One scanner thread stays the default.} Two are 4.5 to 16 \% slower on all four corpora, with 4 to 9 \% more CPU and 140 to 310 MiB more memory; when the decision was taken they were level on Init and Std and 13 \% slower on navier-stokes-euler. The faster the loader thread scans itself, the less a helper has to give, and the tapes of the helpers replay record by record.}
\li{\strong{No scanner thread at all, with a plain read, is level with one} (-1.3 to +1.2 \%, inside the scatter of two rounds). The mapping and its 96,000 page faults per Mathlib pass (section 3) neither gain nor lose against the kernel copying the file into the buffer; nothing speaks for changing the rule.}
}
}
}

